WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.399
Three forces end this inheritance.

2
00:00:02.399 --> 00:00:05.421
NTLM is going: Microsoft
has deprecated it,

3
00:00:05.421 --> 00:00:08.874
and the program has
committed to eliminating it.

4
00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:14.339
Zero trust needs the Entra identity
plane in front of every human sign-in.

5
00:00:14.339 --> 00:00:17.236
And when Active Directory
stops being the source,

6
00:00:17.236 --> 00:00:19.902
the engine needs an
identity that outlives it.

7
00:00:19.902 --> 00:00:24.328
April first, 2027 is the
program's own NTLM block date,

8
00:00:24.328 --> 00:00:27.449
not a Microsoft or federal deadline.

9
00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:32.983
The outside dates in 2027 are support dates
for older Windows Server and SQL Server,

10
00:00:32.983 --> 00:00:36.041
and none of those versions
can take Entra logins.

11
00:00:36.041 --> 00:00:40.618
So the decision is to hold the
order: count and consolidate,

12
00:00:40.618 --> 00:00:43.670
enable Arc, move logins, then block NTLM.

13
00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.460
Counting comes first.
